{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mr7oqxjf153","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Run 27 repair storm root cause: healthy window gate included the failing tail","summary":"Run 27 fired 6 slow qwen REPAIRs (mostly 60-120s timeouts) on a WHOLE recalled program that finished at live pass rate 1.0, leaving only 13 actions in the 1500s budget and starving the LLM-free exploration phase. Root cause: _handle_divergence in ewm/agent.py gated repair on _live_pass_rate() computed over the rolling window that ALREADY INCLUDED the current failing transition (appended in _record_transition BEFORE the divergence handler runs). Early in a game, before the window fills with passes, a single isolated transient drags the small-window rate below repair_trigger_pass_rate (0.85), so window_holds is False and repair fires on a model that is actually healthy. Fix (Run 28): added _prior_window_healthy() which measures health over the window EXCLUDING the failing tail (the same \"healthy JUST BEFORE this divergence\" test _try_tolerate_transient already uses) and applies it to WHOLE programs too; when it holds, repair is suppressed and the loop routes to the LLM-free exploration/reactive path (telemetry repair_suppressed_healthy). Also added a consecutive-LLM-timeout backoff: _decide classifies timeout LlmErrors, counts consecutive ones, and after config.repair_timeout_backoff (default 2) latches _repair_backoff_tripped so _handle_divergence stops entering REPAIR for the rest of the game (telemetry llm_timeouts, repair_timeout_backoff_tripped). Guard is transient-only: a persistent defect degrades the prior window and still repairs (verified against the Run-13 wall-mover test). Full ewm suite 379 passed + --smoke green.","category":null,"tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-07-05T11:06:03.723Z","vec":[-0.04204317182302475,0.005177167244255543,0.027282357215881348,0.036859724670648575,0.07022515684366226,-0.05708739906549454,-0.06771138310432434,0.06639009714126587,-